**Latest update:** cosmetic shake and its editor controls have been removed at your request. Older evidence videos may still show it.

# Merge Chamber

A complete local browser simulator based on the supplied `1000067745.mp4`. TypeScript, Canvas 2D, and Planck physics. Nothing is uploaded to a server. The app contains no external fonts, CDN scripts, or runtime network dependencies.

## Launch the finished app

**Windows:** extract the project ZIP, then double-click **Launch.cmd**. Keep its console open while playing. It uses installed Node.js, or the bundled Codex Node runtime if available on this computer.

**Any desktop with Node.js:** run `node scripts/serve.mjs --open` in this folder, then open **http://127.0.0.1:4173**. The included `dist/` is already built; no dependency installation is needed to play. Node.js 22 is suitable for both playing and development.

The reference stream starts immediately. Click **Enable sound** once to unlock browser audio. Space pauses/resumes; Reset restores the initial nine-object stream. **Restart empty chamber** is under Motion & feed.

Always use the same address and port to access the same saved browser setup. `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, different ports, and different browsers have separate storage.

## Finish & save a video

Open **Finish a video** above Merge progression. Choose a portrait resolution (540p, 720p, 1080p, 1440p or 4K), 24/30/60 FPS, 1–300 seconds, Standard/High/Ultra quality, MP4 or WebM, and whether to include game sounds. Click **Finish & save video**. The preview pauses while a separate fresh simulation renders from the initial stream using the applied project settings. It does not capture the current pile or record changes made during rendering. Apply pending tier/geometry changes before exporting.

Every video frame is rendered at the chosen resolution and assigned an explicit timestamp. Physics advances in fixed 1/120-second steps and waits for encoding. A slow computer takes longer to finish instead of losing frames. Sound is mixed offline from the same collision, merge and spawn events, with custom tier sounds, volumes, mute, threshold, cooldown and voice limits. Live audio does not need to be unlocked for export. Include game sounds honors mute; unmute the project if you want audible output.

Keep the page open until it finishes. Progress shows frame count and estimated time; **Cancel render** keeps the project and previous completed video intact. The finished video downloads automatically and **Download finished video** remains available after reload in this browser. If automatic download is blocked, click that link. The preview stays paused afterward; press Resume to continue.

Export options save with the project. **Export project** backs up the editable settings and actual image/audio assets; import that ZIP to render again later. The latest finished video is stored separately in browser file storage and is not inside the editable project ZIP. Download it for a permanent copy; clearing browser data removes the local copy. Encoding writes to disk incrementally and mixes sound in one-second blocks rather than keeping a whole raw video in RAM.

Use current desktop Chrome or Edge at the localhost address. Format/resolution support depends on the browser's encoder; unsupported choices show an error and never silently lower resolution or FPS. 4K output cannot invent detail absent from low-resolution uploaded pictures. MP4/WebM use lossy video compression; High and Ultra increase the bitrate. This is frame-complete offline rendering, not a claim of mathematically lossless video. Browser suspension may delay rendering; resuming the page continues from the next frame. Closing the page interrupts an unfinished render (the project remains saved); partial renders are not resumable.

See [evidence/offline-motion.mp4](evidence/offline-motion.mp4) for a 12-second export with sound, and [evidence/video-tests.json](evidence/video-tests.json) for decoded frame/duration checks. Run `node tests/video-browser.cjs` with the development server running to repeat export verification.

## Customize without code

- **Username:** edit the Username field near the top of the editor. The default is `@povanimationsim`, drawn subtly in the center of the chamber like the second reference video. Uncheck **Show username in the middle** or clear the field to remove it. Changes apply live and save with your project, including complete ZIP export/import. The watermark is also included in clean view and finished videos when enabled.

- **Pictures:** open Merge progression, expand a tier, and choose Replace image. PNG and WebP transparency is preserved; JPEG, GIF, AVIF and BMP are also accepted if the browser decodes them. GIF is treated as an image rather than a physics animation. The image keeps its aspect ratio. Use the single **Size (px)** field to resize the picture and hitbox together, then click **Apply size & restart**. There are no separate picture-size or hitbox-size controls. Optional X/Y offsets are under the collapsed **Picture position** section. Circular crop is optional; the default uses the cutout silhouette. Pictures now rotate with their physical bodies, following the second supplied video. Untouched feed starts unspun. Motion & feed includes a rotation toggle and Spin damping.
- **Sizes and progression:** edit **Size**, move tiers earlier/later, add tiers, or remove them. **Apply size & restart** (or the shared **Apply & reset**) safely restarts the chamber with your pending changes. The first tier must fit in the chute. Final-tier objects stay and collide; they do not merge into a nonexistent tier.
- **Physics:** Motion & feed exposes gravity, Object bounce, independent Wall bounce, Merge expansion bounce, friction, damping, spawn interval, feed speed and simulation speed. Use **Apply reference bounce & restart** to apply the updated, lighter-gravity motion to an existing saved setup without replacing its images, sounds, sizes or geometry. This restarts the chamber. Defaults are gravity 170, object bounce 0.9, wall bounce 0.98, expansion bounce 1.5, friction 0.015 and damping 0.03. Growing merges push only where they touch another body or wall; there is no free-space launch impulse. The untouched feed moves at a constant speed, as measured in the reference. Gravity applies after first contact. There are no random velocity kicks. A subpixel deterministic spawn offset avoids perfectly symmetric stacking.
- **Geometry and effects:** Outline color 1 and Outline color 2 choose the two solid halves (electric violet and icy mint by default), including the chute. They apply live and save with the project. Chamber & effects controls the circle, neck width, two-color outline, glow, rings, sparkles and duration. Cosmetic sprite shake has been removed; pictures follow their physical positions and rotation. Geometry requires Apply & reset. Other effect edits apply live. Existing saved projects gain the default shake automatically on reload without resetting their physics or assets.
